{{ steps "Review your order" "review" }}

Nothing has been ordered yet and nothing has left your wallet.

{{- /*
The order itself, full width.

Rows with a picture rather than a bulleted list, matching the order page a
buyer reaches next: the thing they are checking is that this is the right
order, and a thumbnail answers that faster than a line of words.
*/}}

--panel[full=on, padding=14, margin=0 0 10 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
{{range .Items}}
--listing--
title: {{ .Product.Title }}
summary: {{ .Quantity }} × {{ money .Product.Price }}
meta: {{ money .Total }}
{{ with productImage .Product.Image }}image: {{.}}
{{ end -}}
--/listing--
{{end}}
### Total: {{ money .Total }}{{ with .TotalDCR }} · ≈ {{.}}{{ end }}
--/panel--

{{- /*
The two settled facts, each the width of the order they are about.

Side by side they were two half-width notes with no relationship to each
other or to the order above them. In a row, with the mark on the right, the
thing a buyer is checking and the way to change it sit at opposite ends of
one line.
*/}}

--paysummary[icon={{if eq .Checkout.Method "onchain"}}onchain{{else}}lightning{{end}}, label=Paying with, value={{ with .MethodSays }}{{.}}{{ else }}The seller will be in touch{{ end }}, link=/checkout, linklabel=Change]--

{{if eq .Delivery "post"}}
{{- /*
The note about how the seller reaches you lives behind the question mark.

It is true, worth knowing once, and read every time by everybody who already
knows it -- which is what a help icon is for. It follows Hide help text under
Appearance, like the app's own.
*/}}
--panel[full=on, padding=14, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8, help=A phone number is only for whoever delivers this. The seller reaches you in Bison Relay, in this order's own messages.]--
**Posted to**

{{ address .Checkout.Ship }}

[Change](/checkout)
--/panel--
{{else if eq .Delivery "file"}}
--panel[full=on, padding=14, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
**Delivered here**

{{if gt (len .Files) 1}}These arrive{{else}}This arrives{{end}} as a file from
the seller, in Bison Relay, once your payment lands. Nothing is posted, so
there is no address to give.
--/panel--
{{else}}
--panel[full=on, padding=14, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
**How you get it**

Nothing in this order is posted or sent as a file. The seller arranges it
with you in the order's own messages, which are at the bottom of the order
page once it is placed.
--/panel--
{{end}}

{{if .TotalDCR}}
--panel[full=on, padding=12, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
The {{ .TotalDCR }} is worked out at today's rate the moment you place the
order, and holds for {{ .QuoteHoldsFor }}. If it lapses before you pay, the
shop quotes it again — nothing is lost and nothing is charged.
--/panel--
{{end}}

{{- /*
One press, and it goes straight through to the pay page.

There was a confirmation dialog on this, which asked the buyer to agree to
the amount a second time on a page whose whole purpose is checking the
amount. Two asks for one decision is not twice as careful; it is a step
somebody has to read to find out it says nothing new. What this press does is
reversible -- an unpaid order can be called off from the order itself, and
nothing has been charged -- so the page it leads to is the answer, not a box
in front of it.
*/}}

--form--
type="action" value="/placeOrder"
type="submit" label="Place order" style="primary"
--/form--
